SDRk corrections of the llvm-mca 23.1.1 scheduling models (decision D942, 2026-11-08).

Apply in the root of llvm-project-23.1.1.src with `patch -p1`. Only numbers of the
models that SDRk's cycle simulation uses are changed, from measured or documented values:

- x86 (skylake, znver2, znver3, alderlake, znver4, sapphirerapids): uops.info
  instructions.xml of 2026-03-29, SHA-256
  e5e702caaf04c4fc1f75192a9bbe4d8554b3e174f7933a14d124cc33ca677ab3 (sapphirerapids
  takes the values of EMR, the closest core uops.info measures).
- cortex-a72 (simulated with the A57 model): Arm Cortex-A72 Software Optimization
  Guide, ARM UAN 0016A, SHA-256
  b74576514a8e4ee3be567cc5d9884cc9a70ae59e4411542da2c77375c7c40c4c.
- cortex-a76 (simulated with the Neoverse N1 model): Arm Neoverse N1 Software
  Optimization Guide, PJDOC-466751330-9707 issue 4.0, SHA-256
  275bc255ed5b33874531bc4aa626fd3ad72d9066ac571bd43c3158de970edf7f.

Every changed or added definition carries an `SDRk:` comment with its source. The
only additions beyond numbers: one store resource in the Znver2 model (as Znver3 and
Znver4 have) and one FP divider resource in the Alder Lake P and Sapphire Rapids
models (as the Skylake model has).

